module

public import Mathlib.Algebra.MvPolynomial.Eval
public import TauCeti.LowDimTopology.Heegaard.MinusDifferential

/-!
# The full multi-pointed differential of a Heegaard diagram

A multi-pointed Heegaard diagram of a knot or link carries several basepoints, the `w`'s and the
`z`'s. Its full complex is generated by the generators of the diagram over the polynomial ring with
one variable for each basepoint, and its differential counts the Whitney disks `φ` of Maslov index
one, recording their multiplicity at every basepoint separately:

`∂ x = ∑_y ∑_φ (∏_b X_b ^ n_b(φ)) y`.

This file sets up these counts for the abstract region incidence data
`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem` with a finite set of basepoints, counting nonnegative domains in
place of holomorphic disks, as the hat and minus differentials of
`TauCeti.LowDimTopology.Heegaard.HatDifferential` and
`TauCeti.LowDimTopology.Heegaard.MinusDifferential` do.

* The **full coefficient** `H.fullCoefficient χ x y : MvPolynomial Basepoint (ZMod 2)` is the sum
  of the monomials `∏_b X_b ^ n_b(D)` over the nonnegative domains `D` of Maslov index one from `x`
  to `y` (`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.minusDomains`). When there are finitely many, its
  coefficient of a monomial is the number, modulo two, of these domains with the multiplicities
  given by its exponents (`coeff_fullCoefficient`).
* The **full differential** `H.fullDifferential χ` is the linear endomorphism of the free module
  on the generators over `MvPolynomial Basepoint (ZMod 2)` with these coefficients.

The other differentials are specializations of the variables.

* For a doubly pointed diagram, the full coefficient is the knot coefficient, and the knot
  differential is the full differential (`TauCeti.LowDimTopology.Heegaard.Knot.Differential`,
  which derives its basic API from the one here).
* Setting every variable to `U` gives the minus coefficient, which records the total multiplicity
  at the basepoints (`aeval_X_fullCoefficient`, and on chains `mapRange_aeval_X_fullDifferential`).
* Setting every variable to `0` gives the hat coefficient (`constantCoeff_fullCoefficient`, and on
  chains `mapRange_constantCoeff_fullDifferential`).

For a knot or link the variables of the `w`'s are kept. Setting the variables of the `z`'s to
`1` gives the filtered differential, which counts the domains with any multiplicity at the `z`'s;
setting them to `0` gives its associated graded differential, which counts only those with
`n_z = 0`.
Evaluation at an arbitrary family of values is `aeval_fullCoefficient` (or
`aeval_fullCoefficient_of_finite` when finitely many domains are counted), and on chains
`mapRange_fullDifferential_apply`. For the multi-pointed diagram of a grid diagram these two
specializations are the filtered and the unblocked grid differentials
(`TauCeti.LowDimTopology.Heegaard.Grid.MinusDifferential`).

As for the other differentials, these are counts of domains rather than of holomorphic disks, and
they agree with the holomorphic counts only for diagrams in which each counted domain carries
exactly one holomorphic disk modulo translation; neither that condition nor the agreement is
formalized here, nor is `∂ ∘ ∂ = 0`. In an infinite set of counted domains the coefficient is `0`
by the convention of `finsum`, and the results below carry the finiteness hypotheses under which the
count has the properties listed.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.fullCoefficient`: the sum of `∏_b X_b ^ n_b(D)` over the
  nonnegative domains of Maslov index one.
* `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.fullDifferential`: the full multi-pointed differential.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.coeff_fullCoefficient`: the coefficients count domains by their
  multiplicities at the basepoints.
* `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.aeval_fullCoefficient` and
  `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.aeval_fullCoefficient_of_finite`: evaluating the variables.
* `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.aeval_X_fullCoefficient` and
  `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.constantCoeff_fullCoefficient`: the minus and hat coefficients.
* `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.mapRange_fullDifferential_apply`,
  `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.mapRange_aeval_X_fullDifferential` and
  `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.mapRange_constantCoeff_fullDifferential`: the same on chains.

## References

* P. Ozsváth and Z. Szabó, *Holomorphic disks, link invariants and the multi-variable Alexander
  polynomial*, Algebr. Geom. Topol. **8** (2008),
  [arXiv:math/0512286](https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0512286), §3 (multi-pointed diagrams of links
  and their complexes).
* I. Zemke, *Link cobordisms and functoriality in link Floer homology*, J. Topol. **12** (2019),
  [arXiv:1610.05207](https://arxiv.org/abs/1610.05207) (the full link Floer complex, with one
  variable for each basepoint).
-/

public section

open MvPolynomial

namespace TauCeti

namespace HeegaardRegionSystem

universe u v w

variable {n : ℕ} {Point : Type u} {Region : Type v} {Basepoint : Type w}
  {H : HeegaardRegionSystem n Point Region Basepoint}

variable [Fintype Point] [DecidableEq Region] [Fintype Region]

section Coefficient

variable [Fintype Basepoint]

variable (H) in
/-- The coefficient of the generator `y` in the full multi-pointed differential of the generator
`x`: the sum of the monomials `∏_b X_b ^ n_b(D)` over the nonnegative domains `D` of Maslov index
one from `x` to `y`. This is meaningful when the set `H.minusDomains χ x y` of these domains is
finite; for an infinite set the coefficient is `0`. -/
noncomputable def fullCoefficient (χ : Region → ℤ) (x y : H.Generator) :
    MvPolynomial Basepoint (ZMod 2) :=
  ∑ᶠ D ∈ H.minusDomains χ x y, ∏ b, X b ^ (D (H.basepoint b)).toNat

variable {χ : Region → ℤ} {x y : H.Generator}

theorem fullCoefficient_def : H.fullCoefficient χ x y =
    ∑ᶠ D ∈ H.minusDomains χ x y, ∏ b, X b ^ (D (H.basepoint b)).toNat :=
  (rfl)

/-- When finitely many domains are counted, the full coefficient is a finite sum. -/
theorem fullCoefficient_eq_sum (hfin : (H.minusDomains χ x y).Finite) :
    H.fullCoefficient χ x y = ∑ D ∈ hfin.toFinset, ∏ b, X b ^ (D (H.basepoint b)).toNat :=
  finsum_mem_eq_finite_toFinset_sum _ hfin

/-- When infinitely many domains are counted, the full coefficient is `0`. -/
theorem fullCoefficient_eq_zero_of_infinite (h : (H.minusDomains χ x y).Infinite) :
    H.fullCoefficient χ x y = 0 :=
  finsum_mem_eq_zero_of_infinite <| by
    rwa [Set.inter_eq_left.mpr fun D _ => Function.mem_support.mpr <| by
      rw [prod_X_pow, Ne, monomial_eq_zero]
      exact one_ne_zero]

/-- The full coefficient vanishes when no domain is counted. -/
theorem fullCoefficient_eq_zero_of_minusDomains_eq_empty (h : H.minusDomains χ x y = ∅) :
    H.fullCoefficient χ x y = 0 := by
  simp [fullCoefficient_def, h]

/-- The coefficient of the monomial `∏_b X_b ^ m b` in the full coefficient from `x` to `y` is the
number, modulo two, of counted domains from `x` to `y` with multiplicity `m b` at each basepoint
`b`. -/
theorem coeff_fullCoefficient (hfin : (H.minusDomains χ x y).Finite) (m : Basepoint →₀ ℕ) :
    (H.fullCoefficient χ x y).coeff m =
      {D ∈ H.minusDomains χ x y | ∀ b, D (H.basepoint b) = m b}.ncard := by
  classical
  rw [fullCoefficient_eq_sum hfin, coeff_sum]
  simp only [prod_X_pow, coeff_monomial, Finset.sum_boole]
  rw [← Set.ncard_coe_finset]
  congr 2
  ext D
  simp only [Finset.coe_filter, Set.Finite.mem_toFinset, Set.mem_ofPred_eq]
  refine and_congr_right fun hD => ?_
  rw [DFunLike.ext_iff]
  refine forall_congr' fun b => ?_
  have hb := basepoint_nonneg_of_mem_minusDomains hD b
  simp only [Finsupp.indicator_apply, Finset.mem_univ, dite_true]
  omega

/-- A nonzero coefficient of the monomial `∏_b X_b ^ m b` in the full coefficient from `x` to `y`
comes from a counted domain from `x` to `y` with multiplicity `m b` at each basepoint `b`. -/
theorem exists_mem_minusDomains_of_coeff_fullCoefficient_ne_zero {m : Basepoint →₀ ℕ}
    (h : (H.fullCoefficient χ x y).coeff m ≠ 0) :
    ∃ D ∈ H.minusDomains χ x y, ∀ b, D (H.basepoint b) = m b := by
  by_cases hfin : (H.minusDomains χ x y).Finite
  · rw [coeff_fullCoefficient hfin] at h
    exact Set.nonempty_of_ncard_ne_zero fun h0 => h (by rw [h0, Nat.cast_zero])
  · simp [fullCoefficient_eq_zero_of_infinite hfin] at h

/-- Evaluating each variable `X_b` at an element `g b` of an algebra, the full coefficient becomes
the sum of `∏_b g b ^ n_b(D)` over the counted domains, when there are finitely many. -/
theorem aeval_fullCoefficient_of_finite {S : Type*} [CommSemiring S] [Algebra (ZMod 2) S]
    (g : Basepoint → S) (hfin : (H.minusDomains χ x y).Finite) :
    aeval g (H.fullCoefficient χ x y) =
      ∑ᶠ D ∈ H.minusDomains χ x y, ∏ b, g b ^ (D (H.basepoint b)).toNat := by
  rw [fullCoefficient_eq_sum hfin, map_sum, finsum_mem_eq_finite_toFinset_sum _ hfin]
  simp

/-- Evaluating each variable `X_b` at an element `g b` of an algebra, the full coefficient becomes
the sum of `∏_b g b ^ n_b(D)` over the counted domains, provided none of the products
`∏_b g b ^ m b` vanishes. -/
theorem aeval_fullCoefficient {S : Type*} [CommSemiring S] [Algebra (ZMod 2) S]
    (g : Basepoint → S) (hg : ∀ m : Basepoint → ℕ, ∏ b, g b ^ m b ≠ 0) :
    aeval g (H.fullCoefficient χ x y) =
      ∑ᶠ D ∈ H.minusDomains χ x y, ∏ b, g b ^ (D (H.basepoint b)).toNat := by
  by_cases hfin : (H.minusDomains χ x y).Finite
  · exact aeval_fullCoefficient_of_finite g hfin
  · rw [fullCoefficient_eq_zero_of_infinite hfin, map_zero, finsum_mem_eq_zero_of_infinite]
    rwa [Set.inter_eq_left.mpr fun D _ => Function.mem_support.mpr (hg _)]

/-- **Setting every variable to `U` gives the minus coefficient.** Evaluating every variable at
`X`, the full coefficient becomes the minus coefficient, which records the total multiplicity of a
domain at the basepoints. -/
@[simp]
theorem aeval_X_fullCoefficient :
    aeval (fun _ => Polynomial.X) (H.fullCoefficient χ x y) = H.minusCoefficient χ x y := by
  by_cases hfin : (H.minusDomains χ x y).Finite
  · rw [aeval_fullCoefficient_of_finite _ hfin, minusCoefficient_def]
    refine finsum_mem_congr rfl fun D hD => ?_
    have h : ∑ b, D (H.basepoint b) = ((∑ b, (D (H.basepoint b)).toNat : ℕ) : ℤ) := by
      push_cast
      exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun b _ =>
        (Int.toNat_of_nonneg (basepoint_nonneg_of_mem_minusDomains hD b)).symm
    rw [h, Int.toNat_natCast, Finset.prod_pow_eq_pow_sum]
  · rw [fullCoefficient_eq_zero_of_infinite hfin, map_zero,
      minusCoefficient_eq_zero_of_infinite hfin]

/-- **Setting every variable to `0` gives the hat coefficient.** When finitely many domains are
counted, the constant coefficient of the full coefficient is the hat coefficient: the counted
domains with multiplicity zero at every basepoint are those counted by the hat differential. -/
theorem constantCoeff_fullCoefficient (hfin : (H.minusDomains χ x y).Finite) :
    constantCoeff (H.fullCoefficient χ x y) = H.hatCoefficient χ x y := by
  rw [constantCoeff_eq, coeff_fullCoefficient hfin, hatCoefficient_def,
    hatDomains_eq_setOf_mem_minusDomains]
  simp

end Coefficient

variable {χ : Region → ℤ} {x y : H.Generator}

section Differential

variable [Fintype Basepoint]

variable (H) in
/-- The full multi-pointed differential of a Heegaard diagram with region Euler characteristics
`χ`: the linear endomorphism of the free module on the generators over
`MvPolynomial Basepoint (ZMod 2)` whose coefficient from `x` to `y` is the sum of the monomials
`∏_b X_b ^ n_b(D)` over the nonnegative domains `D` of Maslov index one from `x` to `y`
(`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.fullCoefficient`). -/
noncomputable def fullDifferential (χ : Region → ℤ) :
    (H.Generator →₀ MvPolynomial Basepoint (ZMod 2)) →ₗ[MvPolynomial Basepoint (ZMod 2)]
      H.Generator →₀ MvPolynomial Basepoint (ZMod 2) :=
  Finsupp.linearCombination _ fun x => Finsupp.equivFunOnFinite.symm (H.fullCoefficient χ x)

/-- The matrix coefficients of the full differential are the polynomials
`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.fullCoefficient`. -/
@[simp]
theorem fullDifferential_single_apply (x y : H.Generator) (a : MvPolynomial Basepoint (ZMod 2)) :
    H.fullDifferential χ (Finsupp.single x a) y = a * H.fullCoefficient χ x y :=
  Finsupp.linearCombination_equivFunOnFinite_symm_single_apply _ x y a

/-- The coefficient of `y` in the full differential of a chain `c`. -/
theorem fullDifferential_apply (c : H.Generator →₀ MvPolynomial Basepoint (ZMod 2))
    (y : H.Generator) :
    H.fullDifferential χ c y = c.sum fun x a => a * H.fullCoefficient χ x y :=
  Finsupp.linearCombination_equivFunOnFinite_symm_apply _ c y

/-- The full differential vanishes exactly when all of its coefficients vanish. -/
theorem fullDifferential_eq_zero_iff :
    H.fullDifferential χ = 0 ↔ ∀ x y, H.fullCoefficient χ x y = 0 :=
  Finsupp.linearCombination_equivFunOnFinite_symm_eq_zero_iff

/-- **Specializing the variables in the full differential.** Applying a ring homomorphism `f` to
the coefficients of a chain, the coefficient of `y` in the image of the full differential is the
sum of the coefficients of the image of the chain, multiplied by the images under `f` of the full
coefficients. -/
theorem mapRange_fullDifferential_apply {S F : Type*} [CommSemiring S]
    [FunLike F (MvPolynomial Basepoint (ZMod 2)) S]
    [RingHomClass F (MvPolynomial Basepoint (ZMod 2)) S] (f : F)
    (c : H.Generator →₀ MvPolynomial Basepoint (ZMod 2)) (y : H.Generator) :
    Finsupp.mapRange f (map_zero f) (H.fullDifferential χ c) y =
      (Finsupp.mapRange f (map_zero f) c).sum fun x a => a * f (H.fullCoefficient χ x y) := by
  rw [Finsupp.mapRange_apply, fullDifferential_apply, map_finsuppSum,
    Finsupp.sum_mapRange_index fun _ => zero_mul _]
  simp only [map_mul]

/-- **Setting every variable to `U` gives the minus differential.** Evaluating every variable at
`X` in the coefficients of a chain intertwines the full differential with the minus differential. -/
theorem mapRange_aeval_X_fullDifferential (c : H.Generator →₀ MvPolynomial Basepoint (ZMod 2)) :
    Finsupp.mapRange (aeval fun _ => (Polynomial.X : Polynomial (ZMod 2))) (map_zero _)
        (H.fullDifferential χ c) =
      H.minusDifferential χ
        (Finsupp.mapRange (aeval fun _ => (Polynomial.X : Polynomial (ZMod 2))) (map_zero _)
          c) := by
  ext y
  rw [mapRange_fullDifferential_apply, minusDifferential_apply]
  simp only [aeval_X_fullCoefficient]

/-- **Setting every variable to `0` gives the hat differential.** When the counts are finite,
taking constant coefficients of a chain intertwines the full differential with the hat
differential. -/
theorem mapRange_constantCoeff_fullDifferential (hfin : ∀ x y, (H.minusDomains χ x y).Finite)
    (c : H.Generator →₀ MvPolynomial Basepoint (ZMod 2)) :
    Finsupp.mapRange constantCoeff (map_zero _) (H.fullDifferential χ c) =
      H.hatDifferential χ (Finsupp.mapRange constantCoeff (map_zero _) c) := by
  ext y
  rw [mapRange_fullDifferential_apply, hatDifferential_apply]
  simp only [constantCoeff_fullCoefficient (hfin _ y)]

end Differential

end HeegaardRegionSystem

end TauCeti
